{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/941658-looking-for-advice-on-letting-a-player-play-a-gargoyle","id":941658,"title":"Looking for Advice On letting a player play a Gargoyle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-01T20:59:33-07:00","id":941658,"title":"Looking for Advice On letting a player play a Gargoyle","content":"I have a few players that really want to play gargoyles. so I'm creating modified kindred creation rules. I was looking for advice on what you guys might suggest. So far I've been playing with the idea that gargoyles can operate only till sun down or sun rise. So you can be a day gargoyle or a night one. You can be a created one or even rarer a wild gargoyle.<br /> <br /> I'm currently creating clans of gargoyles based on the kindred clans and one for wild ones. <br /> <br /> Any advice on what there power pool should be. I was playing with the idea of kindred blood but maybe it should be something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T23:05:47-07:00","id":941719,"title":"","content":"Hmmm..Interesting proposition. Are you thinking a playable version of the Requiem Monster - Guardians created by blood magic, or closer to the Gargoyles from the Disney cartoon?<br /> <br /> If you are thinking more like the cartoon, you may be able to strip-mine some ideas from the Classic WoD fan supplement posted <a href=\"http://gamingnerdsrus.co/bjz/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divi